WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.217
An information system is not just an
application.

2
00:00:03.217 --> 00:00:05.196
Imagine a customer places an order.

3
00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:10.354
A person confirms the request, a process
defines what should happen next, data records

4
00:00:10.354 --> 00:00:16.249
the facts, and technology moves that record to
the people who fulfill and monitor the order.

5
00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:20.312
A useful system coordinates all four parts
around a business outcome.

6
00:00:20.426 --> 00:00:24.044
The order becomes useful only when its data is
trustworthy.

7
00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:30.074
Required fields are validated, identifiers
connect related records, and business rules

8
00:00:30.074 --> 00:00:31.718
prevent impossible states.

9
00:00:31.718 --> 00:00:36.169
The same reliable record can support
inventory, billing, customer service, and

10
00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:40.619
fulfillment without each team inventing a
different version of what happened.

11
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.561
Managers do not need every database row.

12
00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:48.395
They need a decision view: are orders late,
where do exceptions occur, and which change

13
00:00:48.395 --> 00:00:49.684
would improve the outcome?

14
00:00:49.684 --> 00:00:54.152
A dashboard summarizes evidence, but people
still interpret it in context.

15
00:00:54.152 --> 00:00:59.314
Their decision can revise staffing, inventory
rules, or the process itself.

16
00:00:59.314 --> 00:01:05.119
That feedback loop is the purpose of MIS: use
information to improve how the organization

17
00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:05.506
works.
